# Curated LogScale queries — `humio-packages` catalog

commercetools keeps saved LogScale queries, dashboards, and alert definitions in
`commercetools/humio-packages`. Prefer these over hand writing a query.

- Repo. `commercetools/humio-packages` (private, use `gh`).
- LogScale org. `ctp-eu` at `https://cloud.humio.com/ctp-eu`.
- This rotation package. `{{LOGSCALE_PACKAGE}}`.

## Fetch the live set

```bash
gh api repos/commercetools/humio-packages/contents/{{LOGSCALE_PACKAGE}}/queries --jq '.[].name'
gh api "repos/commercetools/humio-packages/contents/{{LOGSCALE_PACKAGE}}/queries/<file>.yaml" -H "Accept: application/vnd.github.raw"
```

Fetch the exact `queryString` live before presenting it. The catalog below is a
fast reference, not the source of truth.

## Field conventions

| Field | Use |
|---|---|
| `#environment` | `prod` |
| `#cloud_provider.account` | environment selector, parameterized as `?account` |
| `#cloud_provider.service` | `k8s` or `loadbalancer` |
| `kubernetes.pod_namespace` | the rotation namespace |
| `kubernetes.container_name` | the service container, exclude `vault-agent-init` |
| `logLevel` | `error` |
| `http.status_code` | `>= 500` |
| `duration` | request duration in seconds |

`?account` is a parameter. Substitute the concrete account for the environment.
See Environments in `runbook-sources.md`. `*-production-*` matches all prod.

